    {
      "name": "Dybuk Creation",
      "type": "trait",
      "_id": "tFUa7O2SIkT2Jraf",
      "img": "modules/impmal-core/assets/icons/blank.webp",
      "system": {
        "notes": {
         "player": "",
          "gm": "<p>Dybuks are lesser daemonhosts, created as alternatives to risky and unmastered rituals. This profile uses the Cult Fanatic profile as a base: add 1d10+10 to WS, Str, Tgh, and 1d10 to Ag and Wil; add +2d5 Wounds; reduce Int by 1d10 and halve the previous being's Fellowship. Lose all Int-based skill advances, grant two advances in Awareness, one in Reflexes (Dodge), and one in Stealth (Move Silently). Grant a +1d5 bonus to Armor as a Force Field akin to Daemons; unarmed attacks lose the Ineffective trait. Dybuks gain the Tenacious and Frenzy Talents if they don't already have them, plus a 50% chance of 1d5 Mutations (rerolling inappropriate results), and may take results from the Daemonhost Unholy Changes table.</p>"
        },
